│ 6 to 46 and from 6 to 45 per 100,000 pregnancies), and the number of unnecessary terminations (from 16 to 26 and     │
│ from 16 to 25 per 100,000 pregnancies). CONCLUSIONS Contingent screening, with a first trimester cut-off value for   │
│ high risk of 1 in 9, is the preferred option for prenatal screening of women for pregnancies affected by Down\'s     │
