│ association between FMF angle and NT, nasal bone length, or fetal heart rate was shown (P > 0.05). But the FMF angle │
│ was significantly greater in the trisomy 21 fetuses (89.7 vs 82.8, P < 0.001). The intraobserver and interobserver   │
│ agreement were assessed in 9.5% (n = 21) normal cases. Mean (SD) differences of two observers were -0.83 (2.69)      │
│ degrees (P > 0.05). For each observer, mean (SD) differences between the two paired measurements were -0.98 (3.11)   │
│ degrees and 0.93 (1.80) degrees , respectively (P > 0.05). CONCLUSION Our results indicated that measurement of the  │
