cases were from older pregnancies (> or = 35 years old), rates were recalculated with the United States age distribution
of live births to get a more representative estimate of false positives and detection efficiency. RESULTS The median 
free beta-human chorionic gonadotropin and pregnancy-associated plasma protein A levels in cases of Down syndrome was 
